<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isma'il Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830–1895</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ismail the Magnificent, Khedive Ismail</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isma'il Pasha was a grandson of Muhammad Ali who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 1863 and received the title khedive from the Ottoman sultan in 1867. He modernised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, expanded railways and education, opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> in 1869 and extended Egyptian rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. His huge debts led to European financial control, and he was deposed in 1879.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isma-il-pasha.jpg" alt="Isma'il Pasha" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isma%27il_Pasha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
